---
import BaseLayout from "../../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import CodeBlock from "@/components/CodeBlock.astro";
import fs from "node:fs";
import path from "node:path";

const snippetDir = path.join(process.cwd(), "src", "snippets", "kishi");

const vagrantSnippet = fs
    .readFileSync(path.join(snippetDir, "vagrant.txt"), "utf-8")
    .trim();

const lxcSnippet = fs
    .readFileSync(path.join(snippetDir, "lxc.txt"), "utf-8")
    .trim();
---

<BaseLayout title="OverTheWire: Kishi">
    <h2
        class="text-3xl font-normal text-neutral-500 mt-6 mb-4 border-b border-neutral-700 pb-2"
    >
        [RELEASED] Kishi (HES2013 and NSC2013)
    </h2>

    <p class="leading-6 mb-4">
        This wargame was introduced at the <a
            href="http://hackitoergosum.org/"
            class="text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-300 no-underline"
            >Hackito Ergo Sum (HES)</a
        > 2013 and <a
            href="http://nosuchcon.org"
            class="text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-300 no-underline"
            >No Such Con (NSC)</a
        > 2013 conferences in Paris and is centered around the <strong
            >fictictious North-Korean cyberops training facility Kishi</strong
        >
    </p>

    <p class="leading-6 mb-4">
        As of December 2014, the Kishi game has been released to the public and
        can be downloaded through <a
            href="https://www.vagrantup.com/"
            class="text-neutral-500 hover:text-neutral-300 no-underline">Vagrant</a
        > for VirtualBox by typing:
    </p>

    <CodeBlock code={vagrantSnippet} />

    <p class="leading-6 mb-4">
        Kishi listens on ports 22, 80 and 2222, which are forwarded from the VM
        host through ports 6622, 6680 and 3322 respectively. Kishi uses several
        LXC containers internally, you can access them from the host VM through
    </p>

    <CodeBlock code={lxcSnippet} />

    <p class="leading-6 mb-4">
        The SSH server running on port 2222 can be used to login to kishi itself
        with username/password vagrant/vagrant. All containers run an SSH server
        with an admin account with username/password otw/otw. These admin
        accounts are not part of the game and should only be used for setting up
        or debugging. Change their passwords if you connect the VM to a public
        network.
    </p>

    <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
        To start the game, visit Kishi's web server on port 80 (or port 6680 of
        the host).
    </p>
</BaseLayout>
